  "version": "0.7.1-beta.2",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.7.1-beta.1`\n\n### Features\n\n- make each tab in the bar hold its own split layout, as iTerm2 and Windows Terminal do: a split tab showed in the tab bar and again in every pane group's tab strip, so the same session sat in two rows of tabs; now a tab of the bar holds one or more panes laid out by its own split tree, the bar shows it once with its pane count and the marks of all its panes, and each pane of a split tab gets a slim header that names it and splits, zooms, unsplits or closes it; dragging a pane moves it beside another or, onto the tab bar, out into a tab of its own, dragging a tab onto a pane merges its panes there, a pane zooms like tmux on Mod+Alt+Enter, Mod+Alt+\\\\ now unsplits a tab into one tab per pane, the close chord closes the active pane and closing a tab of several sessions asks first; Dockview gives way to a layout of our own that keeps every pane mounted and sized while hidden, so switching tabs or moving panes between them never remounts or refits a terminal, and sessions save the layout in a new format, moving older Dockview layouts over on restore ([2e75e196](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/2e75e1968e661fc0bbb2a6fe9857696312c7310e))\n\n### UI and usability\n\n- mark the active pane of a split tab the way the tab bar marks its active tab: a 2px strip down the header's left edge was easy to miss, so the header now draws what runs in the pane as a tab of its own, which in the active pane takes the active tab's fill and a top accent only as wide as its title, capped at 320px, instead of a stripe across the whole pane ([cca6f84a](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/cca6f84a330b09c3a8f811d08de2d36a17602923))\n\n### Other changes\n\n- read FreeBSD tick groups with as_chunks: clippy 1.99 flags chunks_exact with a constant size, and the fixed-size groups also let each one destructure into its five states instead of indexing ([bcef8c42](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/bcef8c422514aa5a78410437c807abecc43780a2))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.7.1-beta.1...v0.7.1-beta.2](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.7.1-beta.1...v0.7.1-beta.2)",
